        <p>• WARRINGTON UNION.- PERSONS WILL- ING to CONTRACT for the 'supply of any of the Undermentioned articles from Micivelmas to Lady Day next, t„._a be delivered free of expense at the Warrington Union Workhouse, or at the Cottage Homes,Padgate, at such times and in such quantities as the Board of Guardians shall direct, are requested to send in TBNDERS properly sealed, ',indorsed and tree of expense, addressed to the Clerk of the tinardians. before four o'clock p.m. on TUBSDAY, the 20th 'lay of SIOTBMBER, 1901. The following are the articles for which TBNDBRS are required : beef and Provisions Coal, Slack and Gas Coke zieef and Mutton Milk for a year, Workhouse .. Joints for Officers Cottage Homes Flour and Canadian pin head Shoes, Clogs and Slippers; , meal Glazing Loaves of Bread for Sltcols Brushes Straw and Potatoes Coffins brapery ta, Leather Cord and Twill ,Sarnples of any of the above may be seen on application to the Master of the Workhouse. The Coal and Slack supplied ',Rust be to the satisfaction of the House and Schools Coin- lnittees. The Pit and quality of coal must be named in the Tender. Forms of tender and full particulars as to the Probable quantities of each article required may be obtained at the Clerk's Office. Each tender must be made upon ths prescribed form and Properly enclosed and endorsed with • the name of the article lersdered for. Each article tendered for must be of size material Qnd quality shown at the Workhouse. No tenders for other articles will be accepted. Bach aontractor must be prepared (if required) to enter into security for the due performance °f his contract. The Guarlians do not bind thlraseives to accept the lowest or any t.n ler. .11( contract accounts wilt e paid quart• rly. —By order, JAMBS CLOWBS SUTTON, Clerk to the Guardians,</p>
        <p>newsey Chambers, Wsrrington. Ang us. 31st 1904.</p>
