        <p>and balsams were extracted from these won- derful herbs, and eventually a combination was secured which possessed not only healing properties of an unusually high order, but also proved a wonderful soother and powerful antiseptic. Now in its perfected state, Zam-Buk is so pure and wholesome that it may be used upon the most sensitive skin and by the most delicate invalid without harm. Ladies add it to their toilet on account of its Pleasant power of softening and whitening the skin. An injury or sore a, slanted with Zarn--Buk becomes at once cleansed and freed from all foreign subatances that may be irritating the skin; and the healing balsams are naturally absorbed, and become</p>
