      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-09-10_WidnesExaminer_art0108" n="art0108">
        <p>more than this, the check side cannot bring the ball into baulk owing to the second cushion beingjAtruck at too much of an angles The reason that the first cushion must be struck so far inside baulk is because, owing to the intense side necessary for the success of the stroke, the ball would come too much out of baulk were the cushion struck at all near the baulk line. In a similar manner it is possible, by aiming at a cushion about 12 inches out of baulk, to cause a ball to just enter baulk and then go out of baulk again. (To be Continued.)</p>
        <p>Mr. Riso Levi will be pleased fo answer in these columns all questions relative to the _article appearing weekly, and as far as possible any questions on 'other points in connectin Ivith the game of Billiards. Envelopes should be marked "</p>
