        <p>VALUAB FREi.HOLD SHOP PROPERTY IN HORSHMARICHT STREET, WARRINGTON. TO BR SOLD BY AUCTION 137 f ESSRS. THOMAS surro &amp;N I) SONS AT IV JL THE LION HOTEL, BRIDGE STREET, WAR- RINGTON, ON WEDNESDAY THE 218 T. DAY OF SEPTEMBER, 1904 at 5 o'clock in the afternoon precisely, subject to the conditions of Sale to be then and there produced ALL THAT LARGE AND COMMODIOUS SHOP with the Offices. Warehouses, Store-rooms, Workshops, and premises situate at the corner of Horsemarket street and Lyme street, Warrington, and known as " JUBILEE BUILDINGS." The tenure is freehold, subject to a yearly rent-charge of £75 and to certain covenants and conditions. The property comprises 505 1/9 square yards or there- abouts snd has a frontage to Horsemarket-street of 55 feet 0 inches and a frontage to Lyme-street of 56 feet 1 inch; 111 feet 7 inches in all. It occupies one of the most valuable and commanding positions in the tow”, being very advantageously situated within a few yards of Market Gate aud the Public Market, and two or three minutes'walk from the Central Station (Cheshire Lines Hallway) and the Electric Car. The premises are New and Substantially built and afford ample accommodation for carrying on an extensive business, or they could readily be subdivided into four or five large shops. There are four storeys and large dry cellars. For further particulars, plans and conditions of sale, and to view apply to the Auctioneers, Legh Street, Warrin,ton, to Arthur Bennett. Esq.. Chartered Accountant, Market- Gate Chambers, Warrington ; to Messrs. J E. Wright, Garnett &amp; Wright, Surveyors. Warrington or to MESSRS. DAVIES &amp; FORSHAW, Solicitors, Suez Street, Warrington.</p>
